+---
+id: task-002-record-createdat-and-updatedat-on-tasks
+type: task
+title: "Record createdAt and updatedAt on tasks"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Record createdAt and updatedAt on tasks
+
+## Request
+
+The app should show how old a task is, and what changed recently. Each task records when it was created
+and when it was last changed.
+
+- Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, as ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are the same.
+- Every change to a task (completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging it) sets its `updatedAt`
+  to the time of the change.
+
+## Feature and story
+
+- Feature: creation and last-change times on tasks in the Tidy Tasks list.
+- Story: as an app screen, I show how old a task is and what changed recently, from its timestamps.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+1. `add` returns a task whose `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are ISO-8601 date-time strings, and are equal.
+2. `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag` and `untag` each set `updatedAt` to the time of that change, and
+   leave `createdAt` as it was.
+3. A change made later carries a later `updatedAt` than the change before it.
+4. `get`, `find` and `list` return the timestamps as they were last set.
+5. Existing behaviour is unchanged apart from the two new fields.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- R1. `Task` carries `createdAt: string` and `updatedAt: string`, both ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- R2. The time comes from a clock given to the list from outside the domain; the domain code under
+  `src/domain/` reads no clock (directive r3).
+- R3. `createTodoList` in `src/index.ts` takes the clock, defaulting to the current time, so the app
+  keeps calling it with no arguments.
+- R4. A successful `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag` or `untag` sets `updatedAt` to the clock's time.
+  A failed call changes nothing.
+- R5. The doc comments of the changed exports say what the timestamps are.
+- R6. The tests in `test/list.test.ts` cover the acceptance criteria above with a fixed clock, and
+  `npm test` passes.
+
+## Notes for the next steps
+
+- Choice made here: every successful call of a change method sets `updatedAt`, including a call that
+  leaves the task as it was (for example, tagging with a tag it already has). The task's operations are
+  what the request names as changes.
+- Tests that compare a whole `Task` by `deepEqual` will need the two new fields, which the fixed clock
+  makes predictable.
